<title>BRAZIL: Most Brazil markets closed for New Year's holiday.</title>
<headline>Most Brazil markets closed for New Year's holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian stock markets and banks will be closed on Tuesday for the New Year's holidays but interbank dollar-real currency markets will be opened half a day, traders said.</p>
<p>All markets will be closed Wednesday, New Year's Day, and will reopen on Thursday.</p>
<p>Traders said they expect only light trading on Tuesday morning in the commercial and floating rate dollar-real currency markets.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
